    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0570" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51/381</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Messrs. Marvin &amp;
                        Pleasants</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    letter of December 29, 1921, with regard to the flotation of a possible loan to
                    the Government of Greece.</p>
                <p>Inasmuch as the regime now functioning in Greece is not recognized by the
                    Government of the United States, I beg to say that the Department of State could
                    not look with favor upon such a loan.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                            Fletcher</hi>,</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Under
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
